  "notes": "Herdr fork preview (wwelder/herdr): gram entries name the task and folder, and posts reach any pane\n\nSource: 2732613496f3acc5ca3e4f3d613fdcb9e296c679.\n\n- herdr's gram entries (blocked, recap, died) are named after the pane's title (the task, such as \"Assistant feature\") instead of the agent kind, and carry the agent's working directory as `cwd`. A status title such as codex's \"Action Required\" falls back to the agent's name.\n- A Gram an agent sends from its pane carries that pane's `pane_id`, `session` and `cwd`, so HerdrUp files it under the agent with its other entries.\n- `gram.post` takes `pane_id` to address the agent in that pane of the session instead of by name, so agents with no name can be written to as well. A pane-addressed post is visible only to that session's pane, since pane ids repeat across sessions.\n\nAll five assets were built by the manual Build artifacts workflow (run 41948461358).\n\nUpdate with `herdr update` on the preview channel.",
